  <h2>Welcome</h2>
  <p>Welcome to STAND! I’m so excited for your kids to join us and see what they create.</p>
  <p>
    This guide covers everything you need to know before getting started, from drop-off and
    pickup to what to bring and how we work together. If you have any questions, just email us
    at <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Lauren Kassan</strong><br />
    Founder &amp; CEO
  </p>

  <h2>What STAND Is</h2>
  <p>
    STAND is the modern-day lemonade stand. Entrepreneurship is the vehicle, but what kids learn
    along the way is what matters most.
  </p>
  <p>
    Over eight weeks, kids ages 8–13 take an idea and turn it into something real. They’ll learn
    to think for themselves, make decisions, work with others, solve problems, and figure things
    out as they go.
  </p>
  <p>
    We wrap up with Pitch Night, where every kid gets to share what they’ve built with family,
    friends, and guests.
  </p>

  <h2>Before the First Session</h2>
  <p>
    Please complete your child’s profile in Sawyer, including allergies and medical needs,
    emergency contacts, and the names of all adults authorized to pick them up. You’ll also need
    to sign the waiver and choose your photo preferences.
  </p>
  <p>The remaining tuition balance is charged 14 days before the first session.</p>

  <h2>Drop-Off and Pickup</h2>
  <p>STAND is a drop-off program. Please walk your child in and check in with a team member.</p>
  <p>
    Only adults on your pickup list can collect your child. We’ll check their ID the first time
    we meet them. If someone else needs to pick up your child for a particular session, email us
    ahead of time.
  </p>
  <p>
    All kids must leave with an authorized adult. No one can leave alone, walk home, or take a
    rideshare, regardless of age.
  </p>
  <p>
    Running late? Call <a href={URGENT_PHONE.tel}>{URGENT_PHONE.label}</a> so we can let your
    child know.
  </p>
  <p>
    After a 10-minute grace period, late pickups cost $1 per minute. This helps cover the cost of
    having a team member stay with your child until you arrive.
  </p>

  <h2>What to Bring</h2>
  <p>
    A water bottle and a willingness to try things! We’ll provide all the materials kids need to
    create their projects.
  </p>
  <p>
    Please leave valuables at home. Personal devices aren’t allowed during sessions and should
    stay in backpacks.
  </p>

  <h2>How We Work at STAND</h2>
  <p>Five values guide everything we do at STAND.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Say What You Think.</strong> Speak up. Give honest feedback, and be kind about it.</li>
    <li><strong>Make Something Real.</strong> An idea becomes something more when you bring it to life.</li>
    <li><strong>Figure It Out.</strong> Get stuck, try again, and ask for help when you need it.</li>
    <li><strong>Build With Other People.</strong> Your cohort is your team. Make something better together.</li>
    <li><strong>Own It.</strong> Take responsibility for your work, your mistakes, and your wins.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What We Ask of Parents</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Let your kid take the lead.</strong> Cheer them on, ask questions, and give them room
    to figure things out on their own. The messy parts are often where the best learning happens.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Join us for Pitch Night.</strong> It’s a chance to celebrate what the kids have
    created and everything they’ve learned along the way.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>If something doesn’t feel right, tell us early.</strong> We want every kid to feel
    comfortable, supported, and excited to be here.
  </p>

  <h2>When Things Go Sideways</h2>
  <p>
    Sometimes things don’t go as planned. When they don’t, we’ll work through it together.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>A team member will step in and help redirect things in the moment.</li>
    <li>If needed, we’ll have a one-on-one conversation with your child.</li>
    <li>If the issue continues, we’ll talk with you about what’s going on.</li>
    <li>
      If someone’s safety is at risk, we’ll ask you to pick up your child that day. Repeated
      safety issues may mean ending their enrollment.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Bullying, harassment, and physical aggression aren’t tolerated at STAND. These behaviors may
    result in removal from the program, with no refund.
  </p>

  <h2>Health and Safety</h2>
  <p>
    Every session has two adults: a lead instructor running the room and a team member supporting
    check-in, pickup, and anything the kids need. Everyone who works with our kids must pass a
    fingerprint background check.
  </p>
  <p>
    Please keep your child home if they’ve had a fever, been vomiting, or had a contagious illness
    within the past 24 hours.
  </p>
  <p>
    We don’t administer medication except for an EpiPen or inhaler you provide, with a signed
    form.
  </p>
  <p>In an emergency, we’ll call 911 first, then contact you.</p>

  <h2>Photos</h2>
  <p>
    When you enroll, you’ll choose whether we’re allowed to share your child’s photos and work on
    STAND’s channels. We use first names only and never identify a child’s school.
  </p>
  <p>
    If we want to share something with the press, we’ll ask your permission separately each time.
    You can change your photo preferences at any point by emailing us.
  </p>

  <h2>Tuition and Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    A $100 deposit holds your child’s spot and goes toward tuition. The remaining balance is
    charged 14 days before the first session.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you cancel more than 14 days before the first session, you won’t be charged the remaining
    balance. Cancellations within 14 days are non-refundable, and we can’t offer refunds once the
    program begins.
  </p>
  <p>
    If your plans change, you can move to a future STAND cohort, as long as a seat is available.
    We don’t refund or make up missed sessions, but we’ll send you a recap of what your child
    missed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Read the full <a href="/cancellation-policy">Cancellation and Refund Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Communication</h2>
  <p>We’ll send a weekly email with an update on what the kids have been working on and creating.</p>
  <p>
    Have a question? Email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>, and we’ll get back to you
    within one business day. If you need to reach us urgently during a session, call
    <a href={URGENT_PHONE.tel}>{URGENT_PHONE.label}</a>.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
